  "demoScript": "AI is really smart, but it can't read your mind. The more you explain, the more it understands. So here are four things that change everything. First: be specific. Instead of saying write a post, say: write an Instagram post for my bakery, for people who love homemade bread today. Second: give it context. Who are you? Who is it for? And why? Third: tell it the format. Bullets or paragraph? Short or long? Casual or formal? Fourth: if you have an example, send it. One example saves you a lot of words. Last thing: a great prompt isn't magic. It's just clear words."
